From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:54:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: treat a zero NPU stats address as a refusal

When the NPU cannot allocate its flow counters, it still answers the
flow stats setup with success and a zero counter address. The driver
would then map physical address 0 and clear 64 KB there. It now
treats a zero address as a refusal, so offload continues without flow
counters.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c |    8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -365,6 +365,14 @@ static int airoha_npu_ppe_stats_setup(st
 	if (err)
 		goto out;
 
+	/* The firmware reports success with a zero address when its SRAM
+	 * pool has no room left for the counters.
+	 */
+	if (!ppe_data->stats_info.npu_stats_addr) {
+		err = -ENOSPC;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	npu->stats = devm_ioremap(npu->dev,
 				  ppe_data->stats_info.npu_stats_addr,
 				  size);
